), we will first determine the area of the entire isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\) and then subtract the areas of the triangles and rectangle that are not part of the pentagon.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\):**\n   The base \\(AB\\) of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is divided into three segments: \\(AH\\), \\(HF\\), and \\(FB\\). Since \\(HF = 12\\) cm and \\(FB = 6\\) cm, we have \\(AH = AB - HF - FB = 2 \\cdot 18 - 12 - 6 = 18\\) cm.\n   The area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle ABC = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 36 \\times 24 = 432 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of \\(\\triangle ACH\\):**\n   \\(\\triangle ACH\\) is a right triangle with base \\(AH = 18\\) cm and height \\(CH = 24\\) cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle ACH = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 18 \\times 24 = 216 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of \\(\\triangle BCF\\):**\n   \\(\\triangle BCF\\) is a right triangle with base \\(FB = 6\\) cm and height \\(CH = 24\\) cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle BCF = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 24 = 72 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the area of rectangle \\(DEHF\\):**\n   The length of \\(DE = GF = 12\\) cm (since \\(DE = GF\\) and \\(D\\) and \\(G\\) are directly above \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) respectively at the same height of 8 cm from the base).\n   The height of the rectangle is \\(CH - DE = 24 - 8 = 16\\) cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of rectangle } DEHF = 12 \\times 16 = 192 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the area of \\(\\triangle DCH\\):**\n   \\(\\triangle DCH\\) is a right triangle with base \\(DH = 12\\) cm and height \\(CH = 24\\) cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle DCH = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\times 24 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the area of \\(\\triangle HCF\\):**\n   \\(\\triangle HCF\\) is a right triangle with base \\(HF = 12\\) cm and height \\(CH = 24\\) cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle HCF = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\times 24 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate the area of pentagon \\(CDEFG\\):**\n   The area of pentagon \\(CDEFG\\) is the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) minus the areas of \\(\\triangle ACH\\), \\(\\triangle BCF\\), rectangle \\(DEHF\\), \\(\\triangle DCH\\), and \\(\\triangle HCF\\).\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of pentagon } CDEFG = 432 - 216 - 72 - 192 - 144 + 144 + 144 = 216 \\text{ cm}^2.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the area of pentagon \\(CDEFG\\) is \\(\\boxed{216}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{216}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:360"}
